Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:18:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] docs: B3 design rev 3 - as built

What the implementation adds to rev 2 and what it verified (no timing
runs: those are the gates agent's):
- A0 and T1 bit-identical to the base (digests, the 128x15 bot);
  T2 + P3 deterministic; A1 bit-identical to T2 + P3;
- saves on every day of the month continue the whole city bit for bit
  (the continuity town, fields and sha256 on day 91); a save from
  before B3 is the uninterrupted game from its first tick;
- tsc and the full vitest suite clean at b0218df;
- the bot changes by design: 128x15 seed 7 in 2015 is 195,597
  [63452, 94452, 37693] (base 194,432; T2 alone 197,227);
- no systematic tourism shift: on the fixtures without the bot W's
  tourists at each tick are within 0.4 % of B's; the bot's yearly
  tourists differ by its chaos (W / B 0.62-1.14 on 128x15). The base is
  itself below the 0.7-1.3 tourism-jobs band in a young town, so the
  comparison with B decides there;
- T2, P3 and A1 details beyond rev 2 (freshness test, tc / dump
  carried, exports for the calendar test, announce(), the rule wasted
  at d11040 in the prototype and none with P3 under A1);
- the tests that differ from section 7, A1's tests renumbered 11-13
  (rev 2's 6-8 collided with the slicing test 6), the two probes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KT9tXthEhyzExdUuGEecAJ
